## OpenJDK runtime

- Project: Eclipse Temurin / OpenJDK 21 — <https://adoptium.net/>
- License: GNU General Public License version 2 with the Classpath Exception —
  [`licenses/GPL-2.0-with-Classpath-Exception.txt`](licenses/GPL-2.0-with-Classpath-Exception.txt)
- Source: <https://github.com/adoptium/temurin21-binaries>

A `jlink` runtime is embedded in each release binary so users do not need a separate JVM.
The runtime archive keeps the JDK's `legal/` notices; the corresponding source is
available from the Temurin and OpenJDK projects above.

## UnRAR

- Project: UnRAR by Alexander Roshal, used through the `unrar` and `unrar_sys` crates.
- License: UnRAR freeware terms — [`licenses/UnRAR.txt`](licenses/UnRAR.txt)

UnRAR supports `.rar`/`.cbr` chapters. It is used only to read archives; tsuiyomi does not
create RAR files.

## Rust crates

The binary statically links Rust crates under their respective permissive licenses,
including MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib, MPL-2.0, Unicode, CC0, and public-domain
terms. [`licenses/RUST-DEPENDENCIES.txt`](licenses/RUST-DEPENDENCIES.txt) lists every
crate and its license expression, generated from `Cargo.lock` by
`scripts/dependency-notices.py`.

Each crate's full license text and copyright notice are available from its published
package and from <https://crates.io/>. The MIT and Apache-2.0 texts used by most of the
tree are [`LICENSE`](LICENSE) and [`licenses/Apache-2.0.txt`](licenses/Apache-2.0.txt).
